answers.body:
Your code is wrong in the sense that several threads can update the shared resource (namely VSI ) at the same time without synchronisation.
You have therefore a race condition in your parallel loop.
I guess you can fix this with the use of critical OpenMP directive as follow: #pragma omp parallel for shared(N), num_threads(nproc)
for(int i=0;i<N;i++)        //Random Changing of elements of VSI
   {
      int r = RV[i];
      if(r%4 == 0)
          #pragma omp critical
          {VSI[RI[i]].insert(r); VSI[N-RI[i]-1].insert(r);}
      else if(r%4 == 1)
          #pragma omp critical
          {VSI[RI[i]].insert(r); VSI[N-RI[i]-1].erase(r); }
      else if(r%4 == 2)
          #pragma omp critical
          {VSI[RI[i]].erase(r);  VSI[N-RI[i]-1].insert(r);}
      else
          #pragma omp critical
          {VSI[RI[i]].erase(r);  VSI[N-RI[i]-1].erase(r); }
   } I tested this and it seems to work. However, I'm not 100% sure this is correct as this would be the first time for me that I use critical sections inside an if construct this way.
Hope this helps. Gilles

