    for (i2 = 0; i2 < _PB_N; i2++) {
        X[_PB_N-2-i1][i2] = (X[_PB_N-2-i1][i2] - X[_PB_N-i1-3][i2] * A[_PB_N3-i1][i2]) / B[_PB_N-2-i1][i2];
    }
} As long as _PB_N >> nthreads this should work fine. You could also swap the order of the loops like this #pragma omp parallel for private(i1)
for (i2 = 0; i2 < _PB_N; i2++) {
    for (i1 = 1; i1 < _PB_N; i1++) however this will be cache unfriendly. Also, I don't see any reason to use dynamic scheduling. Static scheduling should be more efficient. If you don't specify  the scheduling (like in my code above) the de facto default is static.

