answers.body:
The private clause invokes a default-constructor for class-type variables. In other words, each of your threads operates on a new (empty) instance of std::vector initialized through its default-constructor.
For a copy-construction of the vector you should use the firstprivate clause: #pragma omp parallel firstprivate(objVector)
//                   ~~~~~~~~~~~^ Nonetheless, I suppose you really meant to make this variable a shared one: #pragma omp parallel shared(objVector)
//                   ~~~~~^

