answers.body:
use flat array instead, eg: #define A(i,j) A[i+j*ldA]

for( int j=0; j<n ; j++)
{  
  d= A(k,j) ;
  ...
}

Your loop order will cause a cache miss on every iteration , as you point out. So just swap the order of the loop statements: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)       // now "i" is first
  for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
       a[i][j] = a[i][j] - a[i][k]*a[k][j]; This will fix the row in a and vary just the columns, which means your memory accesses will be contiguous.

