} Edit : well, given the large number of rows, carefully multithreading the reads could actually be possible with minimal false sharing. Note that this makes sense only on a NVME SSD, as SATA SSDs don't really have parallel accesses, and this would even be catastrophic on a HDD. Parallel version for the reads: #pragma omp parallel
    {
        int rowsPerThread = (numRows-1)/omp_get_num_threads() + 1;
        # pragma omp for schedule(static,rowsPerThread)
        for (int row=0; row<numRows; ++row) {
