answers.body:
You just get away with it - you have a race condition that might or might not manifest itself depending on the optimization level at compile time, the thread execution and/or the alignment of the stars. You have to make the push_back() a critical section (i.e use a mutex). For example: #pragma omp parallel shared(Spaces, LookUpTable, BestCoreSpaces) private(LutDistribution, tid)
{
  tid = omp_get_thread_num();
#pragma omp critical
  BestCoreSpaces.push_back( 
    computeBestCoreSpace(tid, &Spaces, &LookUpTable, LutDistribution)
  );
}

